case: d_call_denied_fallback
ac: AC-33 (d), reading per SPEC 5.0 and 12.7
kind: client (browser job), plus one crafted Call
compile: ostrel check exits 0 with no diagnostic
principals: alice, bob (development identities, debug build, AC-12)
given: alice has made Coupon { code: "A10", percent: 10 }; both principals can see it (`see if signed`)
each probe starts in a freshly loaded tab, so the text "shown -1" is visible before the click
probes:
  1. alice, online, clicks "Plain" on A10
     server: call rule c.author == me is true; Return 10
     expect: text "shown 10"
  2. bob, online, clicks "Plain" on A10 (the must deny case)
     server: the row resolves through bob's `see` (D99), then the call rule is false; Return Denied
     expect: text stays "shown -1"; it never shows "shown 0"; the std error notice reports the failure
  3. bob, online, clicks "Named" on A10
     server: Return Denied
     expect: text "shown 0", because `catch Denied` names the kind
  4. bob, offline (`sync.state` is offline), clicks "Plain" on A10
     expect: text "shown 0"; no Call frame is sent, and after reconnect the server has received no Call for it
  5. bob, online, clicks "Plain" on A10 and the connection closes after the Call frame was sent
     expect: the call fails with OutcomeUnknown; text stays "shown -1"; nothing is resent after reconnect
  6. crafted Call by bob, sent directly over the protocol: discount(A10)
     expect: Return Denied
final db: one Coupon row, unchanged by all probes
must not: "shown 0" after probe 2 or probe 5
ASSUMPTION: an unhandled error of a `Remote` value ends the client function at that expression,
  like a failed `check` in SYNTAX 5.2, so the assignment to `shown` does not happen. The binding
  part is only that `shown` never becomes 0 in probes 2 and 5.
